    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0040" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg26"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="44" xml:id="d35-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-18">July 18, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have just written Welles
                    recalling President Ríos statement to me that when relations with the Axis are
                    broken there may be some trouble, which he did not appear to think would be
                    serious, but in the event of such trouble he would “like to think that he would
                    have the support of the United States”. I have suggested to Welles for his
                    consideration whether it would not be helpful were I authorized to say to the
                    President that in the event <pb facs="0041" n="27" xml:id="pg27"/> of trouble
                    due to the breaking of relations he could count on our support.<anchor n="45"
                        xml:id="d35-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>It would seem inevitable anyway since any trouble due to this reason would be on
                    the part of the Nazis, and we can hardly permit them to take over power in Chile
                    in any event. I suspect that Welles will discuss the matter with you.</p>
                <p>With warmest regards,</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Claude G. Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d35-f1" n="44" type="source" xml:id="d35-f1-content">
